  "releaseNotes": "v14.1.0: Major read-path overhaul. Generated and non-generated DAOs now both reach Dapper-class throughput.\n\nNew APIs (Source Generator emits these on entities with primary keys):\n- Task<E> FindByPrimaryKeyAsync(pk..., conn, timeout) — strongly-typed positional args, const SQL, no Dictionary allocation\n- Task<int> DeleteByPrimaryKeyAsync(pk..., conn, timeout) — same pattern for deletes\n\nSource Generator additions:\n- SELECT fast path: const SQL template plus a ToEntityFast override using literal ordinals and typed reader.GetXxx calls (skips SafeGet wrapping)\n- FindBy / Delete fast path: per-DAO ConcurrentDictionary cache of SQL keyed by the sorted key set; the Dictionary entry point routes through it before the QueryBuilder fallback\n- DeleteAll const SQL\n\nCore runtime improvements:\n- Dao<E>.Table now caches the Table<E> instance; EntityVersionType setter invalidates the cache\n- EntityReaderCache<E> compiles a per-(type, version) Func<IDataRecord, ITable, E> via Expression trees, replacing the per-row reflection loop (DelegateCache lookups, GetInterfaces probes, CatchThrow closures) in ToEntityInDefaultWay\n- ConcurrentDictionary cache for Type.GetType(assemblyQualifiedName); SafeGetType also fixes a latent DBNull bug\n- QueryBuilder switches Relay from per-step List copy to a lazily-materialized parent-pointer chain; Merge replaces builder.ToString() per iteration with HasContent + LastCharIsSpace flags and caches Represent() per call\n- s_logger is a static readonly Logger field; Debug calls that build parameter strings are now guarded by IsDebugEnabled\n- OverridedColumns.Count replaces null-check + LINQ Any() in every fast-path guard\n\nPublic surface:\n- IColumn gains a PropertyInfo accessor (used by the compiled reader). External implementations of IColumn need to add it.\n- Dao<E>.s_logger visibility changed from private to protected so generated subclasses can guard their Debug calls.\n\nBenchmark highlights (AMD Ryzen 9 5950X, SQLite, .NET 9):\n- Select 1000 rows, non-generated DAO: 11.6 ms / 5.9 MB -> 2.6 ms / 557 KB\n- Select 1000 rows, generated DAO: 2.4 ms / 836 KB -> 1.8 ms / 436 KB (matches Dapper)\n- FindBy 1000 PK lookups, Typed PK: 158 ms / 2316 KB (beats Dapper at 159 ms / 2495 KB on both axes)\n\nAll 197 existing tests pass plus 3 new TypeCacheTest cases.",
